[
  {
    "id": "c001",
    "name": "Confidentiality of Memorandum",
    "text": "THIS CONFIDENTIAL PRIVATE PLACEMENT MEMORANDUM (THE “MEMORANDUM”) HAS BEEN PREPARED SOLELY FOR PROSPECTIVE INVESTORS ON A CONFIDENTIAL BASIS CONSIDERING THE PURCHASE OF PROMISSORY NOTES (THE “NOTES”) FROM MORTGAGE FUND ‘08 LLC (THE “COMPANY”), ANY REPRODUCTION OR DISTRIBUTION OF THIS MEMORANDUM, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, OR THE DISCLOSURE OF ITS CONTENTS, WITHOUT THE PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT OF THE MORTGAGE FUND LEC, ITS MANAGER (THE “MANAGER\"), IS PROHIBITED. BY ACCEPTING THIS MEMORANDUM, EACH PROSPECTIVE INVESTOR AGREES TO THE FOREGOING."
  },
  {
    "id": "c002",
    "name": "Investor Reliance and Regulatory Disclaimer",
    "text": "IN MAKING AN INVESTMENT DECISION, INVESTORS MUST RELY ON THEIR OWN EXAMINATION OF THE NOTES, THE COMPANY AND THE TERMS OF THE OFFERING, INCLUDING THE MERITS AND RISKS INVOLVED. THE NOTES HAVE NOT BEEN RECOMMENDED BY ANY FEDERAL, STATE OR FOREIGN SECURITIES COMMISSION OR REGULATORY AUTHORITY. FURTHERMORE, THE FOREGOING AUTHORITIES HAVE NOT CONFIRMED THE ACCURACY OR DETERMINED THE ADEQUACY OF THIS DOCUMENT. ANY REPRESENTATION TO THE CONTRARY IS A CRIMINAL OFFENSE."
  },
  {
    "id": "c003",
    "name": "Securities and Investment Company Registration",
    "text": "THE NOTES HAVE NOT BEEN REGISTERED UNDER THE SECURITIES ACT OF 1933, AS AMENDED (THE “ACT”), OR ANY STATE SECURITIES LAWS OR THE LAWS OF ANY FOREIGN JURISDICTION, THE NOTES WILL BE OFFERED AND SOLD UNDER THE EXEMPTION PROVIDED BY SECTION 4(2) OF THE ACT AND REGULATION D PROMULGATED THEREUNDER AND OTHER EXEMPTIONS OF SIMILAR IMPORT IN THE LAWS OF THE STATES AND OTHER JURISDICTIONS WHERE THE OFFERING WILL BE MADE. THE COMPANY WILL NOT BE REGISTERED AS AN INVESTMENT COMPANY UNDER THE INVESTMENT COMPANY ACT OF 1940 (THE “INVESTMENT COMPANY ACT\"). CONSEQUENTLY, INVESTORS WILL NOT BE AFFORDED THE PROTECTIONS OF THE INVESTMENT COMPANY ACT."
  },
  {
    "id": "c004",
    "name": "Restrictions on Transfer and Resale",
    "text": "THE NOTES ARE SUBJECT TO RESTRICTIONS ON TRANSFERABILITY AND RESALE AND MAY NOT BE TRANSFERRED OR RESOLD EXCEPT AS PERMITTED UNDER THE ACT AND THE APPLICABLE STATE SECURITIES LAWS PURSUANT TO REGISTRATION OR EXEMPTION THEREFROM. IN ADDITION, SUCH NOTES MAY NOT BE SOLD, TRANSFERRED, ASSIGNED OR HYPOTHECATED, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, EXCEPT AS PROVIDED IN THE NOTE PURCHASE AGREEMENT REFERRED TO HEREIN. ACCORDINGLY, INVESTORS SHOULD BE AWARE THAT THEY WILL BE REQUIRED TO BEAR THE FINANCIAL RISKS OF AN INVESTMENT IN THE NOTES FOR AN INDEFINITE PERIOD OF TIME. THERE WILL BE NO PUBLIC MARKET FOR THE NOTES, AND THERE IS NO OBLIGATION ON THE PART OF ANY PERSON TO REGISTER THE NOTES UNDER THE ACT OR ANY STATE SECURITIES LAWS."
  },
  {
    "id": "c005",
    "name": "Offering Conditions and Investment Risk",
    "text": "THE NOTES ARE OFFERED SUBJECT TO PRIOR SALE, AND SUBJECT TO THE RIGHT OF THE MANAGER OF THE COMPANY TO REJECT ANY SUBSCRIPTION IN WHOLE OR IN PART. AN INVESTMENT IN THE NOTES WILL INVOLVE SIGNIFICANT RISKS DUE TO, AMONG OTHER THINGS, THE NATURE OF THE COMPANY'S PORTFOLIO LOANS AND THE NATURE OF THE NOTES. THERE CAN BE NO ASSURANCE THAT THE COMPANY’S OBJECTIVES WILL BE REALIZED. INVESTORS SHOULD HAVE THE FINANCIAL ABILITY AND WILLINGNESS TO ACCEPT THE RISKS AND LACK OF LIQUIDITY, WHICH ARE CHARACTERISTIC OF THE INVESTMENT DESCRIBED HEREIN."
  },
  {
    "id": "c006",
    "name": "No Legal, Tax or Investment Advice",
    "text": "PROSPECTIVE INVESTORS SHOULD NOT CONSTRUE THE CONTENTS OF THIS MEMORANDUM AS LEGAL, TAX, INVESTMENT OR OTHER ADVICE. EACH PROSPECTIVE INVESTOR SHOULD MAKE ITS OWN INQUIRIES AND CONSULT ITS ADVISORS AS TO THE COMPANY AND THIS OFFERING AND AS TO LEGAL, TAX AND RELATED MATTERS CONCERNING AN INVESTMENT IN THE NOTES."
  },
  {
    "id": "c007",
    "name": "Projections and Access to Information",
    "text": "THE COMPANY'S MANAGEMENT BASED ALL ESTIMATES AND PROJECTIONS AS TO EVENTS THAT MAY OCCUR IN THE FUTURE UPON THEIR BEST JUDGMENT AS OF THE DATE OF THIS MEMORANDUM (OR THE LATEST AMENDMENT OR SUPPLEMENT HERETO). WHETHER OR NOT SUCH ESTIMATES OR PROJECTIONS MAY BE ACHIEVED WILL DEPEND UPON THE COMPANY’S ACHIEVING ITS OVERALL BUSINESS OBJECTIVES AND THE AVAILABILITY OF FUNDS, INCLUDING FUNDS FROM THE SALE OF THE NOTES. WE DO NOT GUARANTEE THAT ANY OF THESE PROJECTIONS WILL BE ATTAINED. ACTUAL RESULTS WILL VARY FROM THE PROJECTIONS, AND SUCH VARIATIONS MAY BE MATERIAL. PRIOR TO THE SALE OF THE NOTES, THE COMPANY WILL PROVIDE YOU WITH THE OPPORTUNITY TO ASK MANAGEMENT, ITS COUNSEL AND ADVISORS QUESTIONS CONCERNING THE TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF THE OFFERING AND TO OBTAIN ANY ADDITIONAL INFORMATION IN THE COMPANY'S POSSESSION OR WHICH THE COMPANY CAN OBTAIN WITHOUT UNREASONABLE EFFORT OR EXPENSE."
  },
  {
    "id": "c008",
    "name": "Third-Party Information Disclaimer",
    "text": "CERTAIN INFORMATION CONTAINED HEREIN CONCERNING ECONOMIC TRENDS AND PERFORMANCE ARE BASED ON OR DERIVED FROM INFORMATION PROVIDED BY INDEPENDENT THIRD PARTY SOURCES. THE Case: 12-04137 Doc# 75-2 Filed: 09/16/13 Entered: 09/16/13 15:56:26 Page 4 of 40 Case3:14-cv-00993-SI_ Documenti7-1 FiledQ8/05/14_ Page107 of 268 COMPANY BELIEVES THAT SUCH INFORMATION IS ACCURATE AND THAT THE SOURCES FROM WHICH IT HAS BEEN OBTAINED ARE RELIABLE, THE COMPANY CANNOT GUARANTEE THE ACCURACY OF SUCH INFORMATION, HOWEVER, AND HAS NOT INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED THE ASSUMPTIONS ON WHICH SUCH INFORMATION IS BASED."
  },
  {
    "id": "c009",
    "name": "Offering Terms and Modification Rights",
    "text": "THIS OFFERING IS SUBJECT TO THE TERMS DESCRIBED IN THIS MEMORANDUM. THIS MEMORANDUM IS QUALIFIED IN ITS ENTIRETY BY REFERENCE TO THE SUBSCRIPTION AGREEMENT, THE NOTE PURCHASE AGREEMENT, THE NOTES, THE SECURITY AGREEMENT AND RELATED INSTRUMENTS, AND THE COMPANY’S LIMITED LIABILITY COMPANY OPERATING AGREEMENT (COLLECTIVELY THE “OFFERING DOCUMENTS”). NO PERSON HAS BEEN AUTHORIZED IN CONNECTION WITH THIS OFFERING TO GIVE ANY INFORMATION OR TO MAKE ANY REPRESENTATIONS OTHER THAN AS CONTAINED IN THIS MEMORANDUM. STATEMENTS IN THIS MEMORANDUM ARE MADE AS OF THE DATE HEREOF UNLESS STATED OTHERWISE HEREIN, AND NEITHER THE DELIVERY OF THIS MEMORANDUM AT ANY TIME, NOR ANY SALE HEREUNDER, SHALL UNDER ANY CIRCUMSTANCES CREATE AN IMPLICATION THAT THE INFORMATION CONTAINED HEREIN IS CORRECT AS OF ANY TIME SUBSEQUENT TO SUCH DATE. THIS MEMORANDUM DOES NOT CONSTITUTE AN OFFER OR SOLICITATION IN ANY STATE OR OTHER JURISDICTION TO ANY PERSON OR ENTITY TO WHICH iT IS UNLAWFUL TO MAKE SUCH OFFER OR SOLICITATION IN SUCH STATE OR JURISDICTION. PRIOR TO THE FINAL CLOSING OF THE OFFERING, THE MANAGER OF THE COMPANY AND ITS AFFILIATES RESERVE THE RIGHT TO MODIFY ANY OF THE TERMS OF THE OFFERING AND THE OFFERING DOCUMENTS DESCRIBED HEREIN."
  },
  {
    "id": "c010",
    "name": "Termination of Offering",
    "text": "THIS MEMORANDUM WAS PREPARED SOLELY FOR YOU AND OTHER SELECTED POTENTIAL INVESTORS INTERESTED IN THIS PRIVATE PLACEMENT. WE MAY TERMINATE THIS OFFERING AT ANY TIME BEFORE A CLOSING,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c011",
    "name": "Confidential/Trade Secret",
    "text": "CONFIDENTIAL/TRADE SECRET BY TAKENG RECEIPT OF THIS MEMORANDUM, YOU AGREE THAT ITS CONTENTS CONSTITUTE PROPRIETARY AND CONFIDENTIAL INFORMATION THAT THE COMPANY, THE MORTGAGE FUND LLC, BAR-K, INC, B-4 PARTNERS, LLC, AND THEIR AFFILIATES, INVESTMENT FUNDS, COMPANIES, PROGRAMS AND PORTFOLIO LOAN BORROWERS (THE “AFFECTED PARTIES”) DERIVE INDEPENDENT ECONOMIC VALUE FROM NOT BEING GENERALLY KNOWN AND ARE THE SUBJECT OF REASONABLE EFFORTS TO MAINTAIN THEIR SECRECY. THE RECIPIENT FURTHER AGREES THAT THE CONTENTS OF THIS MEMORANDUM ARE A TRADE SECRET, THE DISCLOSURE OF WHICH ARE LIKELY TO CAUSE SUBSTANTIAL AND IRREPARABLE COMPETITIVE HARM TO THE AFFECTED PARTIES OR THEIR RESPECTIVE BUSINESSES. WHETHER OR NOT YOU INVEST IN THESE SECURITIES, YOU MAY NOT DISTRIBUTE THIS MEMORANDUM TO ANYONE OTHER THAN YOUR OWN FINANCIAL AND LEGAL ADVISORS, NOR MAY YOU MAKE COPIES OF THIS OR ANY OTHER DOCUMENT YOU RECEIVE, EXCEPT TO THE EXTENT NECESSARY TO CONSULT WITH YOUR FINANCIAL AND LEGAL ADVISORS WHO ARE ADVISING YOU IN CONNECTION WITH THIS POTENTIAL INVESTMENT (AND ONLY SO LONG AS THEY AGREE TO HOLD THIS INFORMATION CONFIDENTIAL AND NOT USE IT FOR PURPOSES OTHER THAN ADVISING YOU IN CONNECTION HEREWITH). ANY OTHER REPRODUCTION OR DISTRIBUTION OF THIS MEMORANDUM, IN WHOLE OR IN PART, OR THE DISCLOSURE OF ITS CONTENTS, WITHOUT THE PRIOR WRITTEN CONSENT OF THE MANAGER, IS PROHIBITED. BY ACCEPTING THIS MEMORANDUM, EACH RECIPIENT AGREES TO THE FOREGOING,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c012",
    "name": "I. Executive Summary — Offering and Security",
    "text": "I. Executive Summary MORTGAGE FUND °08 LLC (the “Company”), sponsored by the principals of R.E. Loans, LLC, offers a new and attractive opportunity for qualified investors to achieve superior returns with a conservative risk profile through the purchase of promissory notes (the “Notes”) issued by the Company. The Company is targeting to return approximately 8.00% or more per year on the Noteholders investments. The Notes will be secured by the assets of the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c013",
    "name": "Company Formation and Purpose",
    "text": "The Company will be formed as a Delaware limited liability company for the purpose of lending capital raised by the sale of Notes to borrowers (the “Portfolio Borrowers”) to finance the ownership, entitlement, development or rehabilitation of commercial real estate or for other real estate related purposes throughout the United States (the “Portfolic Loans”), The Portfolio Loans will be secured by liens against real property and associated personal property."
  },
  {
    "id": "c014",
    "name": "Management and Servicer",
    "text": "The Company will be managed by its manager, The Mortgage Fund LLC, a California limited liability company formed for this purpose (the “Manager” or “The Mortgage Fund LLC’). The Manager is owned and led by Walter Ng and Kelly Ng (the “Managing Directors” or “Principals”), who together bring to the Company more than 81 years of experience in mortgage lending and investing among them. The Manager expects to hire Bar-K, Inc. to provide Portfolio Loan origination, brokerage and administration services to the Company (“Loan Services”) as “Servicer”, comparable to the services that Bar-K, Inc. provides to R.E. Loans, LLC and that it provided to its predecessor investment funds. Bar-K Inc, is managed by Barney Ng, and owned by Bamey and Kelly Ng. Walter Ng, Kelly Ng and Barney Ng also manage and own, with Bruce Horwitz, M.D., B-4 Partners, LLC, the sponsor of R.E. Loans LLC, and were sponsors of prior investment funds to R.E. Loans, LLC."
  },
  {
    "id": "c015",
    "name": "Subscriptions and Closings",
    "text": "In order to participate in this opportunity, each prospective investor will subscribe to purchase Notes pursuant to a Note Purchase Agreement with the Company by “loaning” their investment capital to the Company (their “Loan Amounts”). Notes will be issued to investors whose subscriptions are accepted by the Company (“Nofeholders”), in its discretion, at the next closing held by the Company, The initial closing is expected to be on or before December 3, 2007, and the Company expects to hold closings on the first day of each calendar month thereafter through May 1, 2009, although there is no assurance that there will be a subsequent closing or that a closing will be held each month, The Company has not targeted a minimum or maximum amount of capital to be raised by a sale of Notes. The Manager, the Principals, their family members, and their affiliates may also purchase Notes on the same terms as the Notes purchased by investors."
  },
  {
    "id": "c016",
    "name": "Interest, Maturity and Payment Terms",
    "text": "The Notes will bear simple interest at a rate determined quarterly by the Managing Directors, subject to a minimum average rate of eight percent (8%) annualized, The Notes will be secured by the assets of the Company. Regardless of when purchased, each Note will have a term ending December 31, 2014, subject, in the discretion of the Company, to a six month extension that would be applicable to all outstanding Notes. Interest will be payable quarterly, but payment of principal will be deferred, at the discretion of the Company, until the maturity of the Note, although principal may be prepaid at any time without penalty."
  },
  {
    "id": "c017",
    "name": "Illiquidity, Prepayment and Transfer Restrictions",
    "text": "The Notes are an illiquid and long-term investment. No investor should subscribe to purchase a Note unless it is prepared to hold the Note until its maturity. Although the Company may, in its discretion, prepay a Note at any time, a Noteholder may not request prepayment of a Note until it has held the Note for a minimum of one year from the date of its issue, and the granting of such request is within the sole discretion of the Company. The Notes will not be transferable except under very limited circumstances and then only in the discretion of the Manager. There is no secondary market for sale of the Notes and none is expected to develop."
  },
  {
    "id": "c018",
    "name": "Status of Noteholders",
    "text": "By virtue of their ownership of the Notes, the Noteholders will be secured creditors of the Company. The Noteholders will not own a membership interest, profit sharing or other direct or indirect equity interest in the Company. The Noteholders should expect to receive IRS Form 1099's issued by the Company with respect to their investments,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c019",
    "name": "Use of Capital and Senior Borrowings",
    "text": "In addition to raising capital for Portfolio Loans, the Company may raise capital from the sale of Notes to pay its expenses, including organizational expenses, to reimburse the Manager for other Company related expenses, and to pay compensation, as more particularly described in the Summary of Principal Terms in this Offering Memorandum, although the Managing Directors expect that such expenses and compensation will generally be covered by the revenues of the Company. The Company may also raise capital for Portfolio Loans or for Company operating and other expenses by borrowings from institutional or other lenders, and such borrowings may be secured by liens on the Company’s assets that are senior to the lien securing the Notes."
  },
  {
    "id": "c020",
    "name": "II. Private Mortgage Lending — Investment Policy",
    "text": "II. Private Mortgage Lending The Company intends to invest in conservatively underwritten real estate mortgage loans with borrowers who are experienced in real estate operations and finance by directly controlling the sourcing, funding and administration of such loans based upon criteria the Principals have found to be successful in the past. The Company will not operate in the sub-prime mortgage market and will not source loans for the purpose of resale. Instead, it will focus the portfolio on loans secured by quality real estate for generation of income to the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c021",
    "name": "Past-Performance Disclaimer",
    "text": "To date, the Principais and their affiliates have a proven lending record of sponsoring investments in welldiversified performing loans that produce solid returns to their investors. To date, no investor has experienced a loss of investment principal through investment vehicles sponsored by the Principals or their affiliates. Although there is no assurance that investors in the Company will experience similar results, the Manager believes that the past real estate lending success of the Principals and their affiliates will generate comparable opportunities for the Company and its Noteholders."
  },
  {
    "id": "c022",
    "name": "Historical Results and Projections Disclaimer",
    "text": "PLEASE NOTE THAT THE COMPANY HAS NO OPERATING HISTORY UPON WHICH TO BASE AN ANALYSIS. THIS SUMMARY AND ANY PROJECTIONS IN THIS MEMORANDUM ARE FOR ILLUSTRATION PURPOSES ONLY. THE RESULTS DESCRIBED IN THIS MEMORANDUM WITH RESPECT TO PREVIOUS -3- CONFIDENTIAL Case: 12-04137 Doc# 75-2 Filed: 09/16/13 Entered: 09/16/13 15:56:26 Page 9 of A8 Case3:14-cv-00993-SI Documenti7-1 Filed08/05/14 Page1ii2 of 268 MORTGAGE LENDING ARE HISTORICAL ONLY, AND WERE INFLUENCED BY AVAILABLE OPPORTUNITIES, DIVERSE MARKET CONDITIONS AND OTHER FACTORS BEYOND THE CONTROL OF THE MANAGER. ANY PROJECTIONS MADE IN THIS MEMORANDUM ARE BASED ON HISTORICAL EXAMPLES AND THE MANAGER’S ESTIMATES OF FUTURE CONDITIONS. THERE IS NO ASSURANCE THAT LENDING OPPORTUNITIES EXPERIENCED BY OTHER INVESTMENT FUNDS IN THE PAST WILL OCCUR IN THE FUTURE, THAT MARKET CONDITIONS WiLL BE AS FAVORABLE TO THE COMPANY AS THEY HAVE BEEN IN THE PAST, OR THAT INVESTORS WILL ENJOY RETURNS ON THEIR INVESTMENT COMPARABLE TO THOSE ENJOYED BY THEM OR BY OTHERS WITH RESPECT TO THEIR PARTICIPATION EN OTHER INVESTMENT FUNDS SPONSORED BY THE COMPANY’S SPONSORS, OR BY OTHERS. THE ACTUAL RESULTS EXPERIENCED BY THE COMPANY WILL DIFFER, AND SUCH VARIATION IS LIKELY TO BE MATERIAL. PLEASE SEE SECTION Vi RISK FACTORS BEFORE DECIDING TO PURCHASE NOTES."
  },
  {
    "id": "c023",
    "name": "III. Management — Manager Duties",
    "text": "Ill, Management The Company will be managed by its Manager, led by the experienced management team of Walter Ng and Kelly Ng as its Managing Directors. In that capacity, they will be responsible for the Company’s operations, lending policies and decisions with respect to the Portfolio Loans."
  },
  {
    "id": "c024",
    "name": "Bar-K Services and Affiliations",
    "text": "They will work closely with Barney Ng, president of Bar-K, Inc. Barney Ng will lead Bar-K in the provision of certain brokerage, origination and administrative services on behalf of the Company in connection with the servicing of its Portfolio Loans. In addition, Walter Ng, Kelly Ng and Barney Ng own and manage affiliated entities engaged in structuring and managing work-outs of troubled mortgage loans and foreclosed properties. Kelly Ng and Barney Ng are the sons of Walter Ng."
  },
  {
    "id": "c025",
    "name": "Servicer Designation",
    "text": "Bar-K, Inc., the Servicer The Manager has selected Bar-K, Inc., an affiliate, as Servicer of the Company’s Portfolio Loans. The Servicer will not take a direct role in the Company’s management. As noted above, Bar-K Inc. is a California corporation that was founded in 1975 (“Bar-K”) by Walter Ng for the purpose of providing certain real estate and related brokerage services with respect to his early lending activities. Bar-K is owned by Barney Ng and Kelly Ng. Since its inception, Bar-K Inc. has originated more than $2 billion of -5- CONFIDENTIAL Case: 12-04137 Doc# 75-2 Filed: 09/16/13 Entered: 09/16/13 15:56:26 Page IL of 48 Case3:14-cv-00993-SI Documenti7-1 Filed08/05/14 Page1ii4 of 268 privately arranged trust deed investments and currently services a Joan portfolio of approximately $795,370,616.00 in mortgage loans on behalf of approximately 2800 individual and _ institutional investors. Bar-K is a real estate broker licensed by the California Department of Corporations and is also a licensed California finance lender and broker."
  },
  {
    "id": "c026",
    "name": "Servicer Duties and Other Clients",
    "text": "The Servicer will originate or arrange all loans acquired by the Company, and will also act as the servicing agent for the Company’s Portfolio Loans. In addition, the Servicer may provide mortgage loan brokerage, administration or other services to other clients, including to R.E. Loans, LLC and to lenders or real estate operators unaffiliated with the Company or its management team."
  },
  {
    "id": "c027",
    "name": "Termination of Manager or Servicer Relationship",
    "text": "The Manager and Servicer retain the right to terminate ail or any portion of their business relationship with the Company at any time, in which event the Company would seek to retain one or more other firms to perform the various services to be rendered by the Manager or Servicer as described below."
  },
  {
    "id": "c028",
    "name": "Compensation Arrangements and Delegation",
    "text": "COMPENSATION TO MANAGEMENT The following discussion summarizes the forms of compensation the Company will pay to the Manager and the Servicer. None of the following compensation was determined by arm’s-length negotiations. The Manager may cause the Company to enter into one or more agreements directly with the Servicer for the provision of Loan Services, or may delegate the performance of all or a portion of such Services to the Servicer by agreement between the Manager and Servicer. If the Company enters into an agreement directly with the Servicer for provision of Loan Services, then compensation outlined below will be paid by the Company to the Servicer. To the extent that the performance of Loan Services is delegated directly by the Manager to the Servicer, compensation owed by the Company with respect to such Services will be paid by the Company directly to the Manager, and the Manager shall be responsible for payments to the Servicer."
  },
  {
    "id": "c029",
    "name": "Portfolio Management Fee",
    "text": "1% annually of the aggregate principal balance of all Portfolio Loans held by the Company, payable monthly (i.e., 0.0833% per month) in advance, based on aggregate principal of Portfolio Loans held on the last day of the preceding month."
  },
  {
    "id": "c030",
    "name": "Loan Servicing Fee",
    "text": "1% annually of the principal amount of each Portfolio Loan, payable monthly (ie., 1/12\" of 1% per month) in arrears, but payable only from Portfolio Loan interest that is received by the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c031",
    "name": "Late Fees",
    "text": "10% of late charges on delinquent Portfolio Loan payments received by the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c032",
    "name": "Default Interest",
    "text": "Servicer will retain any default interest collected from a Portfolio Borrower to the extent it exceeds the regular stated interest rate payable to the Company under the Portfolio Loan."
  },
  {
    "id": "c033",
    "name": "Loan Brokerage, Renewal and Forbearance Fees",
    "text": "Anticipated to average between three percent (3%) and six percent (6%) of the principal amount of the Company’s Portfolio Loans."
  },
  {
    "id": "c034",
    "name": "Documentation and Processing Fees",
    "text": "Anticipated to average approximately $1,000 per loan for documentation and loan processing fees. These fees may vary depending on market conditions."
  },
  {
    "id": "c035",
    "name": "Manager Expenses",
    "text": "Expenses The Manager will bear the operating, legal and administrative expenses of the Company, other than those borne by the Company or Servicer (“Manager Expenses”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c036",
    "name": "Company Expenses and Reimbursement",
    "text": "The Company will bear its organizational fees and costs, taxes, and costs of accounting, audit, investor communications and allocable rent (“Company Expenses”). The Company will reimburse the Manager, the Servicer or any of their affiliates’ amounts expended by them that are Company Expenses."
  },
  {
    "id": "c037",
    "name": "Portfolio Service Expenses",
    "text": "The Servicer will bear the costs associated with the provision of Portfolio Loan Services (“Lean Service Expertses”)."
  },
  {
    "id": "c038",
    "name": "No Fiduciary Responsibility to Noteholders",
    "text": "NO FIDUCIARY RESPONSIBILITY OF MANAGER TO NOTEHOLDERS Under Delaware law, a manager is accountable to a limited liability company’s members as a fiduciary, which means that a manager is required to exercise good faith and integrity with respect to company affairs. This fiduciary duty is in addition to those other duties and obligations of, and limitations on, the Manager which are set forth in the Operating Agreement. At the time of this offering, the Manager is also the sole member of the Company. The Noteholders do not have a member’s interest in the Company, but are solely creditors of the Company. Accordingly, the Manager does not have a direct fiduciary obligation to the Noteholders nor, at the time of this offering, does it have a fiduciary obligation to the Company’s members or contractual obligation under the Operating Agreement independent of its own interests in the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c039",
    "name": "Contractual Covenants to Noteholders",
    "text": "The Company, however, will enter into certain contractual operating covenants and commitments to the Noteholders pursuant to the Note Purchase Agreement, the Notes and the Security Agreement, the breach of which by the Company may give the Noteholders a cause of action against the Company, which would be adverse to the Manager’s interest in the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c040",
    "name": "Manager Exculpation",
    "text": "The Operating Agreement provides that the Manager shall have no liability to the Company for losses resulting from errors in judgment or other acts or omissions, unless the Manager is guilty of fraud, bad faith or willful misconduct."
  },
  {
    "id": "c041",
    "name": "Manager and Servicer Indemnification",
    "text": "The Operating Agreement also provides that the Company shall indemnify the Manager and Servicer against liability and related expenses (including reasonable attorneys’ fees and costs) incurred in dealing with the Company, Noteholders or third parties, so long as no fraud, bad faith or willful misconduct on the part of the Manager or Servicer is involved. A successful indemnification of the Manager or Servicer or any litigation that may arise in connection with their indemnification could deplete the assets of the Company, thereby reducing the assets available to pay the Notes. Therefore, Noteholders may have a more limited opportunity of recovery then they would have absent these provisions in the Operating Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c042",
    "name": "Securities-Law and Creditor Obligations",
    "text": "In addition to its contracted obligations to the Noteholders under the Note Purchase Agreement, the Notes and the Security Agreement, the Company has certain obligations under federal securities laws in connection with the offering and sale of the Notes, the preparation of this Memorandum, and representations to prospective investors and communications to Noteholders regarding the condition of the Company, certain conflicts of interest, and the terms of this offering. There are also certain state and federal laws that govern the respective rights and obligations of the Company with respect to its creditors, and the rights and remedies of a creditor against its obligor."
  },
  {
    "id": "c043",
    "name": "Reliance on Manager",
    "text": "Accordingly, Noteholders must rely on the good faith and integrity of the Manager to comply with the laws, rules and regulations governing the offering of the Notes for purchase, the Company’s relationship with the Noteholder, and to cause the Company to meet its obligations under the Note Purchase Agreement, the Notes and the Security Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c044",
    "name": "Manager Control and Conflicts",
    "text": "The Company’s business operations and affairs will be managed entirely by the Manager, which are subject to certain conflicts of interest. (See “Conflicts of Interest.”)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c045",
    "name": "Conflicts of Interest",
    "text": "CONFLICTS OF INTEREST There are potential conflicts of interest between the Company and the Manager with respect to the activities undertaken by the Manager on the Company’s behalf that benefit the Manager or its affiliates. These conflicts of interest are unlikely to be resolved. The Company has not been separately represented ~8- CONFIDENTIAL of 48 Case3:14-cv-00993-SI Documenti7-1 Filed08/05/14 Page1ii7 of 268 by independent legal counsel in its formation or in its dealings with the Manager and Servicer, and Noteholders must rely on the good faith and integrity of the Manager and Servicer to act in accordance with the terms and conditions of this offering. As noted above, the Manager owes no direct fiduciary obligations to the Noteholders. Any members or managers who may be admitted to the Company in the future may be affiliated with the Manager and may have interests that align more completely with the Manager than with the Noteholders in connection with the Company’s operations. (See “Fiduciary Responsibility of the Managing Member.”’) The following is a list of the important areas in which the interests of the Manager and Servicer will conflict with those of the Noteholders. Except as may arise in the normal course of the relationship, there are no transactions presently contemplated between the Company and the Manager (or its affiliates) other than those listed below:"
  },
  {
    "id": "c046",
    "name": "Loan Brokerage Commissions, Renewal and Forbearance Fees",
    "text": "Loan Brokerage Commissions, Renewal and Forbearance Fees None of the compensation set forth under “Compensation to Management” was determined by arms’ length negotiations. It is anticipated that the loan brokerage commissions, renewal fees and forbearance fees charged to Portfolio Borrowers by the Servicer for most Portfolio Loans will be in the amount set forth herein (see “J/I. Management - Compensation to Management” above), but may be higher or lower depending upon market conditions. Any increase in such charges will have a direct, adverse effect upon the interest rates that Portfolio Borrowers will be willing to pay the Company, thus reducing the overall rate of return to the Company and the Company’s ability to pay the Notes. Conversely, if the Manager or Servicer reduced the commissions and fees charged by it, a higher rate of return on Portfolio Loans might be obtained for the Company, thereby increasing its ability to repay the Notes. This conflict of interest will exist in connection with every Portfolio Loan transaction, and Noteholders must rely upon the terms of the Note Purchase Agreement to the Company, the Notes and the Security Agreement to protect their interests. The Company will generally charge Portfolio Borrowers interest at the rate generally prevailing in the geographical areas where the security property is located for loans to comparable borrowers of similar size, duration and security,"
  },
  {
    "id": "c047",
