  {
    "id": "c052",
    "name": "Allocation of Portfolio Loan Opportunities",
    "text": "Other Funds or Businesses; Allocations of Portfolio Loan Opportunities B-4 Partners LLC, an affiliate of the Manager owned and managed by Walter Ng and Dr. Bruce Horwitz, currently owns and manages R.E. Loans, LLC (‘R.E. Leans”), a licensed California finance lender with a business purpose similar to the Company’s. As of November 2007, R.E. Loans owns a loan portfolio of approximately 60 loans with aggregate principal value of $750 million. R.E. Loans is not anticipated to make additional portfolio loans, but it may take four to six years for its current portfolio to mature or be liquidated. Additionally, in the future, the Manager may also sponsor other funds formed to conduct business similar to that of the Company (together with R.E. Loans, the “Other Sponsored Investment Funds”). If Other Sponsored Investment Funds have capital to loan at the same time as the Company, there will then exist conflicts of interest on the part of the Manager as to whether to offer a particular loan opportunity to the Company or to these other funds. The Manager will decide which loans are appropriate for funding by the Company or by Other Sponsored Funds after consideration of all relevant factors, including the size of the loan, portfolio diversification, remaining term of the Company and the relative amount of uncomnnitted capital available for operations and lending."
  },
  {
    "id": "c053",
    "name": "Other Business Ventures",
    "text": "Also, the Manager may engage for its own account, or for the account of others, in other business ventures, similar to that of the Company or otherwise, and neither the Company nor any Noteholder shall be entitled to any interest therein."
  },
  {
    "id": "c054",
    "name": "Compensation for Outside Activities",
    "text": "The compensation structure applicable to the Manager in connection with loans that are arranged or originated for investors other than the Company or Other Sponsored Investment Funds may be different than the compensation payable by the Company to the Manager for comparable services provided to the Company. Depending on the circumstances at a given point in time, devoting time or effort to provide such services to others than the Company may be more lucrative to the Manager than the compensation payable to the Manager in connection with the Company. As a result, there may exist a financial incentive for the Manager to arrange or originate loans for private investors outside the Company or for Other Sponsored Funds."
  },
  {
    "id": "c055",
    "name": "Reliance on Manager for Note Obligations",
    "text": "Accordingly, the Noteholders must rely on the Manager to act in good faith to cause the Company to meet its obligations to the Noteholders under the terms of the Notes and the Note Purchase Agreement."
  },
  {
    "id": "c056",
    "name": "Allocation of Management Time",
    "text": "Allocation of Management Time The Company will not have independent management and it will rely on the Manager for the operation of the Company. The Manager and its Principals will devote only so much time to the business of the Company as is reasonably required. The Manager and its Principals will have conflicts of interest in allocating management time, services and functions among the Company, existing business interests other than the Company and Other Sponsored Funds which it may organize or other business ventures in which it may be involved. The Manager believes it has sufficient staff available to be fully capable of discharging its responsibilities to all such entities."
  },
  {
