    "name": "Portfolio Borrower Payments",
    "text": "Portfolio Borrowers will make loan payments monthly in arrears, i.¢., with respect to the preceding month, and will be instructed to mail their checks or money orders either directly to the Company or to the Servicer for deposit in the Servicer’s trust account and subsequent disbursement to the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c075",
    "name": "Loans to Related Parties",
    "text": "Loans to Related Parties The Company may make or invest in Related Party Loans, which as noted, may raise significant conflicts of interest. (See “Ji, Management - Conflicts of Interest - Loans to Related Parties”). Aggregate principal amounts of Related Party Loans will not exceed 20% of total Company assets upon the closing of the Related Party Loan in question; making of a Related Party Loan must not be on terms more favorable to the borrower than similar loans negotiated at arm’s-length and must be purchased from the Company by the Manager or its affiliate rf the Loan is in default more than 90 days."
  },
  {
    "id": "c076",
    "name": "Purchase of Loans from Servicer",
    "text": "Purchase of Loans from Servicer The Company will buy or originate most or all of its mortgage loans from or through Servicer, which is in the business of originating and servicing mortgage loans. The Company may also purchase loans from unrelated third parties. Loans purchased by the Company shall not be in default at the time of purchase and must otherwise satisfy the foregoing lending guidelines. Generally, the purchase price to the Company for any such loan will not exceed the par value of the note or its fair market value, whichever is lower, but the Manager may purchase loans from unaffiliated parties for a premium if the Manager believes the total purchase price is fair and reasonable and in the best interests of the Company."
  },
  {
    "id": "c077",
    "name": "Transactions with Sponsored Investment Funds and Private Clients",
    "text": "Transactions between the Company and Sponsored Investment Funds, Private Clients The Company may purchase or sell loans from or to Sponsored Investment Funds, including R.E. Loans, or private Investors doing business with the Manager or its affiliates. The Company may also enter into co-lending transactions including inter-creditor and other agreements for such purpose or to achieve comparable with Sponsored Investment Funds, including R.E. Loans, or private investors or lenders doing business with the Manager or its affiliates. Such transactions will be in compliance with criteria established therefor in the Note Purchase Agreement. In summary, any loan proposed for the Company’s investment that is a purchase from, sale to, of a co-investment with, any such Sponsored Investment Fund or private investor, shali meet all of the relevant Company lending criteria for a non-affiliated loan, shall be priced at fair market value or better for the Company, and shall be on such terms as are customary for the geographical market that is the location of the real property collateral or the borrower, assuming for this purpose an arm’s length negotiation among equal parties, and, if not a new loan, shall be a fully performing loan at the time of its acquisition or co-investment. In the case of a co-investment with a Sponsored Investment Fund or private investor, such co-investment will be on terms no more favorable to such Sponsored Investment Fund or private investor than it is to the Company. Such transactions may involve significant conflicts of interest (See “Ji, Management - Conflicts of Interest - Transactions between the Company and Sponsored Investment Funds, Private Clients”.)"
  },
  {
    "id": "c078",
    "name": "Transactions with Noteholders",
    "text": "Transactions with Noteholders None of the Company, its Manager, principals or affiliates is precluded from (i) selling a property to any Noteholder in connection with a foreclosure, including with purchase financing, or (ii) from making a loan to, purchasing a loan from or entering into a loan or co-lending transaction or activity with any Noteholder, provided that any transaction with a Noteholder that is a Related Party Loan, or with a Noteholder who is also a Sponsored Investment Fund, private investor or lender doing business with the Manager, its Principals or affiliates, must meet the criteria established by the Note Purchase Agreement for such affiliated transactions."
